From 079795e73313b4d9e95aa18c8577a1aa8e1d6aec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:38:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Bugfix: make error handling of `dgraphFold2()` and
 `hdgraphFold2()` collective [report R. Perry and PyScotch]

In non-debug builds, the agreement on local errors at the beginning of
`dgraphFold2()` was compiled out, so a process that failed to allocate
its data returned alone while the other processes posted
communications to it and waited forever.

Moreover, the edge array of normal receivers is allocated after
senders have posted all their sends, since its size depends on the
received edge counts. When this allocation failed, the receiver gave
up without completing its pending receives, whose target arrays were
then freed, and the senders of the edge data were never matched.

Restructure both routines so that:
- the first agreement is always performed, before any communication
  is posted, and also covers graph compaction;
- senders post only the edge count and vertex messages, then all
  processes agree on the allocation of the receiver edge arrays before
  edge data is sent. On failure, all pending communications, which are
  all matched, are completed before buffers are freed;
- all error paths free everything allocated so far, including the
  compacted arrays, the folded data array and the folding data of
  senders, which were leaked before;
- the return value of `MPI_Waitall()` on edge counts is checked.

Debug-mode parameter checks now return immediately, as no clean
collective exit is possible before the folded graph is initialized.

Refs: DGR-01, DGR-22, PS-DGR-4
